.TH "LAGO" "1" "Aug 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-wallets-create-wallet-transaction - Top up a wallet


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago wallets create-wallet-transaction [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
This endpoint is used to top-up an active wallet.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--granted-credits\fP=""
	The number of free granted credits.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create-wallet-transaction

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	Idempotency key for safe mutation retries

.PP
\fB--ignore-paid-top-up-limits\fP=""
	When true, allows topping up the wallet with transactions that exceed the paid top-up limits. Defaults to false.

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	Complete JSON request body or @file.json

.PP
\fB--invoice-custom-section-invoice-custom-section-codes\fP=""
	List of unique codes identifying the invoice custom sections to apply. These override the default invoice custom sections configured at the customer or billing entity level.

.PP
\fB--invoice-custom-section-skip-invoice-custom-sections\fP=""
	Set to 'true' to exclude all invoice custom sections from PDF generation for invoices related to this resource. When 'true', 'invoice_custom_section_codes' is ignored.

.PP
\fB--invoice-requires-successful-payment\fP=""
	A boolean setting that, when set to true, delays issuing an invoice for a wallet top-up until a successful payment is made; if false, the invoice is issued immediately upon wallet top-up, regardless of the payment status. Default value of false.

.PP
\fB--metadata\fP=""
	This optional field allows you to store a list of key-value pairs that hold additional information or custom attributes related to the data.

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	The name of the wallet transaction. It will appear on the invoice as the label for the fee. If not set, the label on the invoice will fallback to either 'Prepaid credits - {{wallet_name}}' if the wallet name is set, or 'Prepaid credits'.

.PP
Note that this name will apply to all transactions ('paid_credits', 'granted_credits' and 'voided_credits') created by this action.

.PP
\fB--paid-credits\fP=""
	The number of paid credits.

.PP
\fB--payment-method-payment-method-id\fP=""
	The unique identifier of the payment method (required when using a specific provider payment method).

.PP
\fB--payment-method-payment-method-type\fP=""
	The type of payment method to use.; one of: provider, manual

.PP
\fB--purchase-order-number\fP=""
	The purchase order number associated with this wallet transaction. It will be added to invoices generated for the resulting wallet top-up. If not set, falls back to the wallet's 'purchase_order_number'.

.PP
\fB--voided-credits\fP=""
	The number of voided credits.

.PP
\fB--wallet-id\fP=""
	Unique identifier assigned to the wallet within the Lago application. This ID is exclusively created by Lago and serves as a unique identifier for the wallet's record within the Lago system.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	Override the Lago API key

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Override the Lago API URL

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	Confirm a dangerous operation with its resource identifier

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print mutating requests without sending them

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Allow insecure HTTP or TLS for self-hosted Lago

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Environment mode: live or test

.PP
\fB--no-retry\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic retries

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, or yaml

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Named profile to use

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath expression applied to the response

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Total request timeout

.PP
\fB--timing\fP[=false]
	Print request latency breakdown

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Print redacted request and response details


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  lago wallets create-wallet-transaction --input @payload.json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlago-wallets(1)\fP
